MODIFICATIONS
-------------

Apache License 2.0, section 4(b) requires derivative works to carry prominent
notices stating that files have been changed. They have been, extensively:

This project is a **translation** of Mattermost server source from Go to Rust.
No file here is a copy of an upstream file. Every Rust module is a
reimplementation of the corresponding Go source, restructured for Rust's type
system, and in a small number of documented cases it deliberately behaves
differently from the original. Those divergences are enumerated in
`docs/TECH_DEBT.md`; the per-file semantics are recorded in `MIGRATION.md`.

Rust source files cite their Go origin in a doc comment, for example:

    //! Port of `server/public/model/channel.go`.

Files under `fixtures/` are generated by running the upstream Go code and
recording its output; they contain no upstream source.


SCOPE OF THIS LICENSE
---------------------

Upstream Mattermost is licensed in two parts. `server/public/`,
`server/templates/`, `server/i18n/` and `webapp/` are under the Apache License
2.0; the remainder of the platform is under the GNU AGPL v3.0, or a commercial
license from Mattermost, Inc.

Everything translated in this repository to date derives from
`server/public/model/`, which is the Apache-2.0 portion. This project is
therefore licensed under Apache-2.0.

**This will have to change.** Phase 2 onward ports `server/channels/store/`,
`server/channels/app/` and `server/channels/api4/`, which are AGPL v3.0. Code
derived from those directories cannot be redistributed under Apache-2.0, so the
project license must move to AGPL-3.0 (or a commercial license must be obtained)
before any of it is committed. This is tracked as a blocking item in
`docs/TECH_DEBT.md`.


